# Learning data safety

Cloud learning data lives in `cloud/taughtStrokes.json`, `cloud/theoryTips.json`, and `cloud/hangulHints.json` (GitHub `main` via Contents API). These are teacher-trained assets.

## Before any learning-data work

1. Copy the three live JSON files (and, if present, `src/data/taughtStrokes.json`) into `_backup_temp/<reason>_<timestamp>/`.
2. Prefer refreshing local `cloud/*.json` from `origin/main` with `git checkout origin/main -- cloud/...` so stale local copies are not pushed.
3. Never overwrite live cloud files with empty, scaffold, or older local content.

## Allowed vs forbidden

- **Allowed:** read-only copies under `cloud/backups/` or `cloud/versions/`; app features that snapshot then restore with explicit user confirm.
- **Forbidden:** casual edits to live JSON; force-push of `main`; Actions/jobs that rewrite live `cloud/*.json` except an explicit, reviewed restore flow.

Version snapshots belong only under `cloud/versions/{taughtStrokes|theoryTips|hangulHints}/` and must never be used as a reason to blank live files.

## Temp backups

Keep `_backup_temp/` local only (gitignored). Do not commit it.
